#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235471 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58606740-b081-5671-ab93-5b28309b7d77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{x}+2x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234683}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58606740-b081-5671-ab93-5b28309b7d77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{x}+2x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234683} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0bd4a86-aed0-5919-98b7-ad23d53bddbe" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235226}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "cfc04756-ffae-5a03-8a05-d0ea5dfb5207" :question/math-academy-id "q-167694" :question/problem "For $x<1,$ ${f}^{′}(x)=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ." :question/worked-solution "For $x<1,$ we use the expression $f(x)={e}^{x}+{x}^{2}+x,$ which is differentiable.\n\nUsing the addition and the power rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x}+{x}^{2}+x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & ={e}^{x}+2x+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
